    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nCreating a tabpage during initialization can leave the original command-line file unloaded, so its window appears empty.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nLoad displayed buffers using temporary window contexts, preserving tab/window selections, alternate tab and directory state. Keep the existing `-p` path and resize the restored tab when a modeline changes screen dimensions.\r\n\r\nFixes #41426.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- Fail-first regression on master `298aea7382` (`bufloaded()` returned 0)\r\n- New Ex/API startup and context-preservation regressions pass\r\n- Startup suite: 85 passed; 2 failures also reproduced on unchanged master core: remote-UI parent connection (sandbox socket wrapper), and existing exrc/restart screen mismatch\r\n- API tabpage suite: 21 passed\r\n- Independent edge probes cover tab/window selection, directory state and BufReadPost mutations\r\n- Debug build, C lint, StyLua, commit lint, and whitespace checks pass\r\n\r\nLocal functional tests use stdio RPC with only the optional test-ID listener suppressed. No test harness changes are committed.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted.",
